  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Related objects are displayed in different places, and their labels can refer to one another.\", \"decision\": \"How should written labels connect related objects?\", \"goal\": \"Help visitors find a satisfying route through the museum while keeping reception and volunteers manageable.\", \"problem\": \"A volunteer-run local museum wants to make a weekend visit easier to navigate. It has a modest collection, printed guides, a reception table, flexible volunteer positions, and several rooms that can remain open independently. The decisions concern interpretation and visitor organization, not conservation rules or safety policy.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nIndividual labels ask a shared question, and a final label draws together the related objects. Visitors compare examples before reading the connecting explanation.\nA shared label explains the relationship first and points visitors to the individual objects. Visitors encounter the connection before comparing the examples.\nEach label names a related object and explains why visitors might look at it next. Connections can guide visitors onward from any starting object."
    }
  ],
